From 73a6e4f3582984c99a341df1a7522646b5690ac2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Han <danielhanchen@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:37:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] FP8 block dequant on ROCm: decode e4m3fn bytes on archs
 without OCP fp8 hardware

On ROCm archs without OCP e4m3fn hardware (gfx1151 and other RDNA3 / RDNA2 / CDNA2 / CDNA3) the
block-scaled e4m3fn weight dequant took either the software-emulated fp8e4nv Triton kernel
(Triton >= 3.5) or the chunked torch loop (older Triton, ragged or rectangular blocks), measured
3x to 10x slower than one pass over the weight on gfx1151. Route those to the byte decoder
_e4m3fn_bytes_dequant, which is bit-identical to both. gfx950 / gfx12, e4m3fnuz / e5m2 weights and
NVIDIA keep their routes. UNSLOTH_FP8_HIP_BYTES_DEQUANT=0 restores the old routing.
